WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:04.740
I deserve some of the blame. I made my farm
scape too inviting.

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:07.280
Okay, this is a mess.

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:08.450
What are we going to do now?

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:10.100
I got your blanket, Mr. Goat.

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:13.970
No no no no no no no. We're going to wait for
Santa Claus by the chimney.

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:17.030
But it's Thanksgiving.

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:19.910
What about Mr. Goat? How come I don't hear him anymore?

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:22.700
Ah, Mr. Goat is fine.

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:24.440
Bahhh!!

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:25.250
Did you hear that?

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:26.960
What is it, Mr. Goat?

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:28.880
Bahh!

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:34.130
He's saying that he needs some time
alone. Look, there's some cookies for Santa here.

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:37.100
Why don't you go and sit by the chimney
and wait?

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:37.110
Santa!

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:42.430
Okay, look, it's not my place to try to
parent your kids.

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:43.110
Good.

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:47.790
But one thing we learned on the farm is that death is a part
of life.

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:50.990
If you tell Joe what happened to that goat, death is
going to be part of your life.

00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:51.330
Okay, you know what?

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:56.550
Kids can handle a lot more than you think.
And every step from birth till the end has

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:58.860
its own magical beauty.

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:02.100
So, do we jam the goat in the garbage or heave
it over the fence?

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:03.300
Teach your children well.

